{
  "id": "mwv-workspace-row-click-nf",
  "priority": "P0",
  "title": "Three windows: each workspace row clicked in each window's sidebar shows in that window, and no other window changes (no film)",
  "why": "Lawrence 2026-10-28 (handoff/multiwindow.md): \"clicking on home/workspaces might bring me to the wrong window\". A row clicked in window N's sidebar must show its workspace in window N (WindowManager.show, origin thisWindow) and leave every other window as it was. Each row is clicked with the pointer (`debug.mouse` at the row's frame from `debug.sidebar_rows`), A, B and A again in each of three windows, and every check reads every window (shown workspace, Home state, rows, panes and tabs, focused pane, frame). The first window, with the earlier journeys' workspaces (its rows may be scrolled), is a fourth window that must not change either.",
  "source": "VIDEO EXTRA item 6 (multi-window), from journeys/p0/mw-workspace-row-click.json",
  "budget_seconds": 210,
  "steps": [
    {
      "do": "new_terminal",
      "via": "key",
      "as": "person",
      "title": "set-up: the person's first terminal (New Terminal key), so the keyboard is in a terminal, not in Home's composer, and a script's newTab shows its workspace"
    },
    {
      "do": "new_terminal",
      "name": "mw-rc-a1-${nonce}",
      "as": "a1",
      "title": "set-up: workspace mw-rc-a1 with a terminal (socket newTab, in the first window)"
    },
    {
      "do": "neutral_prompt"
    },
    {
      "do": "new_terminal",
      "name": "mw-rc-a2-${nonce}",
      "as": "a2",
      "title": "set-up: workspace mw-rc-a2 with a terminal (socket newTab, in the first window)"
    },
    {
      "do": "neutral_prompt"
    },
    {
      "do": "new_terminal",
      "name": "mw-rc-b1-${nonce}",
      "as": "b1",
